<title>UK: Ford confident of Halewood plant subsidy-FT.</title>
<headline>Ford confident of Halewood plant subsidy-FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A senior executive from U.S. car giant Ford has indicated he is confident the future of its Halewood plant in Merseyside, England, is assured, the Financial Times said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Jac Nasser. chairman of Ford of Europe, told the newspaper that talks with the Briitsh government to secure a subsidy were going well.</p>
<p>&quot;We have had very good cooperation from the government. I believe the signs are good. I would say we are on track,&quot; said Nasser.</p>
<p>He added he expected a decision from the government on a grant by the end of the month.</p>
<p>Ford decided in January not to build the next generation of Escort cars at Halewood, putting the assembly plant at risk.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
